# Coach speech (Korean): the rules lesson (level 0, src/coach/lesson.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/lesson.lang.
#
# Placeholders: {your} / {my} = a piece of the player / of the coach ("룩" / "제 나이트": the player's
# pieces carry no possessive word); their particles come from the forms of common.lang ({my:obj} =
# "제 나이트를", {your:cop} = "룩이에요", {your:ins} = "룩으로"), or are invariant ({my}까지, {my}에게).
# {sq}, {sq2}, {to}, {esc} = squares: never a particle after them, always the noun 칸 ("{sq} 칸으로").
# {move:letters} = a move with the scoresheet letters (Korean players write K Q R B N).
# {@}, {@2}, {@3} are invisible marks: the coach points while saying the word right after the mark.
# A ".spoken" key is what the voice says instead: Latin letters and digits in Hangul (a = 에이,
# h = 에이치, e = 이, ranks and points Sino-Korean: 2랭크 = 이 랭크, 3점 = 삼 점, Elo = 엘로).
# Chapter titles are noun phrases said inside events.lang lines ("{chapter}부터 이어서 해 봐요").

# ---- Chapter titles (said inside "Let's continue with {chapter}.") ------------------------------------
lesson.title.welcome = 체스판
lesson.title.pieces = 기물의 움직임
lesson.title.safety = 안전한 잡기와 위험한 잡기
lesson.title.check = 체크
lesson.title.mate = 체크메이트
lesson.title.castling = 캐슬링
lesson.title.en_passant = 앙파상
lesson.title.promotion = 프로모션
lesson.title.draws = 스테일메이트와 무승부
lesson.title.before_move = 두기 전에
lesson.title.opening = 오프닝
lesson.title.etiquette = 실전 게임의 레이팅, 시계, 매너

